{
  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have two RNA-encoder data points at singleprofile/rna_only—pca_n2000 (acc 0.485) and scvi_n200 (acc 0.520)—showing that encoder choice matters (~3.5 pp gap). Image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), so the RNA branch is the primary performance driver. Uncertainty: We have no data on the third RNA encoder, scgpt (a pretrained single-cell foundation model), and it could be substantially better or worse than scvi_n200. Question tested: config_007 (scgpt, singleprofile, rna_only) is a clean single-variable swap from config_004, isolating the RNA-encoder effect with no confounds from profile setting, aggregation, or fusion. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in multiprofile, multimodal, or aggregation/fusion variants, we need to know which RNA encoder to anchor on. Completing the three-way encoder comparison (pca vs scvi vs scgpt) at the simplest setting gives the most information per experiment and prevents us from propagating a suboptimal encoder choice into all downstream multimodal/multiprofile trials."
}

